# Your First Indie Game with Unity

Indie game development lets you create games solo or with small teams. Learn to build, publish, and monetize your own games.

## Why Indie Game Dev?

**Advantages:**
- Full creative control
- Low budget required
- Fast iteration
- Direct player connection
- Keep all profits

**Success Stories:**
- Stardew Valley (solo dev)
- Hollow Knight (3 people)
- Among Us (3 people)
- Celeste (2 people)

## Unity Basics

### Why Unity?

- Free for individuals
- C# programming
- 2D and 3D support
- Cross-platform deployment
- Huge asset store
- Large community

### First Script

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

public class PlayerController : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float speed = 5f;

    void Update()
    {
        // Get input
        float horizontal = Input.GetAxis("Horizontal");
        float vertical = Input.GetAxis("Vertical");

        // Move player
        Vector3 movement = new Vector3(horizontal, vertical, 0);
        transform.Translate(movement * speed * Time.deltaTime);
    }
}
```

